abla p} is computed for each sample based on its distance from the camera. The gradients are then multiplied by this factor. 1. Compute the squared distance: d^2 = \delta{ip}^2. 2. Compute the scaling factor: s{
abla p} = \min\left(1,  rac{\delta{ip}^2}{\sigma^2}ight) If \sigma=1, this simplifies to s{
abla p} = \min(1, \delta{ip}^2). 3. Scale the gradients: 
